# The scripts directory is excluded, with a few exceptions.
#
# `bun install` runs two things out of it: the project's own `prepare`
# lifecycle hook, and the security scanner that bunfig.toml configures.
# Both are hard requirements -- a `prepare` hook that cannot be found fails
# the install, and so does a configured scanner that cannot be found -- and
# neither is optional, so the files have to travel with the build.
#
# The type gate travels with it too. `bun run build` ends with
# `bun run typecheck`, which is `scripts/tsrs.ts` -- and that imports
# `scripts/tsrs-resolve.ts` for the platform lookup. A build that cannot
# find either of them fails at the last step, after the whole compile.
#
# The rest of the directory is development tooling and does not belong in a
# deployment.
#
# The pattern is `/scripts/*` and not `/scripts/` on purpose. A gitignore
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so excluding
# the directory itself would silently exclude these files along with it.
#
# `scripts/verify-deploy-files.ts` checks this list against what the build
# actually needs, so a new script that the build depends on cannot be left
# behind here by accident.
/scripts/*
!/scripts/prepare.ts
!/scripts/security-scanner.ts
!/scripts/tsrs.ts
!/scripts/tsrs-resolve.ts
